  "title": "The Perfectly Timed Toast",
  "family": "fiction",
  "category": "everyday microdramas",
  "premise": "A figure wants butter and toast ready together, but repeatedly prepares one long before the other in an exaggerated kitchen ballet. They arrange the plate, spreader, and butter first, then wait for the toaster’s normal finish signal and assemble one calm breakfast before sitting down.",
  "hook": "The toast is ready. The breakfast is not.",
  "visible_action": "Plate slides late; butter crosses the room; tools collide harmlessly; a simple three-item setup appears; toast pops and is plated.",
  "intended_takeaway_or_theme": "Prepare the nearby steps before the time-sensitive step ends.",
  "gate": "Keep appliances normally used and hands away from slots; no cooking-temperature or food-safety claims.",
